Mon Nov 16 20:33:51 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.6.1:
  * Fixed: output written before the first onData listener is no
    longer lost (#53, #54); the newest 512 KiB of UTF-8, cut only
    between whole characters, is delivered to the first listener
    (and any added in the same tick) just after onData() returns
  * Before, awaiting anything between spawn() and onData() lost the
    shell's first prompt, or all of a fast command's output;
    subscribing in the same tick as spawn() sees no change
  * Repository moved to sursatech/bun-pty; URL and Source0 follow
    the new location (old links redirect)
  * No Rust changes: same vendored crates and same eight dlsym
    entry points, so no consumer rebuild is needed

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov  6 07:40:31 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.6.0:
  * Breaking: Bun 1.4.0 or newer is required (engine-native
    bun:ffi); the JavaScript API is unchanged
  * Length argument of bun_pty_read/bun_pty_write is now usize:
    rebuild any self-built native library pointed to by
    BUN_PTY_LIB from this version
  * write() with an empty string no longer throws on Bun 1.4;
    library load failures now include the dlerror() message
  * Refresh the vendored dependencies (lazy_static 1.5,
    crossbeam 0.8.5, shell-words 1.1.1)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Oct 26 19:27:30 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.5.2:
  * spawn() reports a clear error naming the library path and the
    cause when the native library fails to load, instead of
    `undefined is not an object` (#51); importing without
    spawning keeps working
  * Linux ABI unchanged: same eight dlsym entry points, same
    private librust_pty.so path; no consumer rebuild needed
  * Refresh the vendored dependencies (libc 0.2.190 -> 0.2.191)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Oct 15 05:02:21 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.5.1:
  * Breaking: env is the child's whole environment as in node-pty,
    no longer merged over the parent's (#48); spread process.env
    to keep inherited variables
  * Build the child environment as node-pty builds it: TERM from
    name, PWD from cwd; drop tmux/COLUMNS/LINES on inherit (#49)
  * Leave src/*.test.ts out of the npm package (#50)
  * Linux ABI unchanged: same eight dlsym entry points, same
    private librust_pty.so path; no consumer rebuild needed
  * Refresh the vendored dependencies

